  "prompt": "Build I/O Switch as original zero-build HTML/CSS/JavaScript under the INTRX Stage contract. Match Figma v4 tile 90:604 and stage 90:617. Native geometry in the372×264 reference stage: 120×120 plate at126,52;80×80 recess at146,72;68×36 rocker at152,78;top I and lower O labels remain in their supplied slots;rocker travels38px vertically. Preserve every supplied SVG byte, intrinsic root and captured render offset; CSS paints the captured primitive frames. Use a324×168 fitted native plane at24,20; allow its object shadows to remain visible inside the stage. Native reference starts on; full starts off. Full400×584 retains the complete original368×320 field,79×40 control,34px cap,39px travel and all original materials and copy: {\"title\":\"I/O Switch\",\"description\":\"A 79×40 I/O toggle with a 34px raised pale cap, recessed grey rail and exposed I/O marks\",\"guide\":\"click, drag, or use arrow keys to change the control\"}. Keep the original event program: direction resolves on pointerup from dominant dx versus upward dy, ties choose dy, strict threshold12px, changes increment on every semantic assignment, drag suppresses the next click, cancellation retains the original local coordinates and latch. Use real switch buttons, native Enter/Space, six directional/Home/End keys, pointer capture,44px physical targets, visible focus and live status. Shared Stage owns the Drag Dock action. Normal toggle travel350ms with55% +1px overshoot and80% settle,150ms colour,80ms press and250ms release. Retarget current paint on interruption; reduced motion uses150ms retained opacity fades. Queue intents while held, preserve independent press owners, stop animations while suspended and clean up all listeners, observers, captures and retained paint. No runtime library.",
